@using Ecnanib.DecisionEngine
@using Ecnanib.Shared
@using Ecnanib.WebUi.Pages.Agents

@*
    The team of an agent at work, as a pipeline (FR-ANI-1): each role with the model that it
    was given and the provider of the model, and with what it does now: waiting, working, done,
    or failed. The roles stand in the order that they work in, in three stages: the two analysts,
    which work at the same time, then the Strategist, then the Risk Manager. A stage that the
    work was handed to says so, and the stylesheet draws the line into it: that is the hand-off.

    What a role does is said as a word, so nothing relies on a colour or on what moves
    (FR-THM-5). The marker beside the word is for the eye alone. Everything that moves is in the
    stylesheet, and only for a device that asks for no reduced motion: the page carries no style
    and no script for it. The part is written again over the connection of the page as the cycle
    goes on, and the browser changes the state of a card in its place, which is what lets a
    change be shown as one. With no cycle to show, every role waits.

    The part says that something of it may move for as long as its state lasts, the dot of a
    role that works: the script of the pages has it stand still while the part is off the
    screen (FR-ANI-6). See docs/motion.md.
*@

<ol class="team-pipeline" aria-labelledby="team-heading" data-moves>
    <li class="pipeline-stage">
        @* The two analysts work at the same time, and neither reads what the other answers. *@
        <ul class="pipeline-parallel">
            <li>@Card(Role.MarketAnalyst)</li>
            <li>@Card(Role.SentimentAnalyst)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="@StageOf(Role.Strategist)">@Card(Role.Strategist)</li>
    <li class="@StageOf(Role.RiskManager)">@Card(Role.RiskManager)</li>
</ol>

@code {
    /// <summary>The roles of the team, each with the model that it was given.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IReadOnlyList<LiveRole> Team { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>What each role does in the cycle that the pipeline shows, or null when it shows none: every role waits.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<RoleProgress>? Roles { get; set; }

    /// <summary>What a role does now. A role that the cycle says nothing of waits.</summary>
    private RoleState StateOf(Role role) => Roles?.FirstOrDefault(progress => progress.Role == role)?.State ?? RoleState.Waiting;

    /// <summary>
    /// A stage after the first, which says whether the work was handed to it: its role has
    /// left waiting. The line into it is drawn through then.
    /// </summary>
    private string StageOf(Role role) => LivePages.StageClassOf(handed: StateOf(role) != RoleState.Waiting);

    /// <summary>
    /// A role as a card: its name, its model with the provider, and what it does now. When that
    /// changes, the whole card is read out, so that the word is not said without its role.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment Card(Role role) =>
        @<div class="pipeline-role @LivePages.ClassOf(StateOf(role))" aria-atomic="true">
            <span class="role-name">@AgentPages.Describe(role).Name</span>
            <span class="role-model">@(Team.FirstOrDefault(given => given.Role == role)?.Model ?? AgentReportPages.NoModel)</span>
            <span class="role-state"><span class="role-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>@LivePages.Describe(StateOf(role))</span>
        </div>;
}
